{
  "_comment": [
    "The default local policy: what this machine grants each principal.",
    "",
    "authd reads Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy at every logon. One subkey per",
    "principal, named either by a well-known name or by a literal SID, and each",
    "subkey holds the totality of that principal's authority -- privileges now,",
    "logon rights and more later. Keyed by principal rather than by privilege",
    "because authority scattered across twenty values is authority nobody",
    "audits: `reg ls` on one key answers 'what can this principal do?'.",
    "",
    "!! IF THIS KEY EXISTS AT ALL, IT IS THE WHOLE POLICY. !!",
    "",
    "authd carries a compiled floor, but it applies ONLY when the key is absent",
    "entirely -- it is not merged in per-value. So a partial policy written here",
    "is the complete policy: anything not granted below is not granted. That is",
    "deliberate. The alternative -- a compiled default that each record replaces",
    "-- fails in the wrong direction, because an administrator who writes one",
    "record believing they have locked the machine down would still be handing",
    "out whatever the compiled table said for every principal they did not",
    "mention, from a table they cannot read. Failing towards LESS privilege is",
    "visible (things stop working); failing towards more is not.",
    "",
    "Because this file creates the key, the compiled floor is inert on any",
    "machine that applies it, and can never silently contribute.",
    "",
    "-- Everyone --------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege is not a convenience. Without it a process cannot",
    "traverse a directory to reach a file, so a token lacking it cannot exec a",
    "shell. It is the one privilege whose absence makes a machine unusable, and",
    "it is the only thing in authd's compiled floor.",
    "",
    "SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege is a convenience -- build systems and",
    "packaging tools assume it -- so it ships here but is deliberately NOT in",
    "the compiled floor. That keeps the floor to exactly 'what a logon needs to",
    "function' rather than 'what is nice to have'.",
    "",
    "-- Administrators --------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "The operational set: what administering a machine actually requires.",
    "",
    "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege is repeated here on purpose, and it is insurance",
    "rather than redundancy. Privileges union across every SID on the token, so",
    "if someone edits this key and drops the Everyone record, administrators",
    "keep working and can repair it. Without the repeat, one incomplete edit",
    "would lock every principal on the machine out of exec'ing a shell.",
    "",
    "Integrity is High. Note this machine has no elevation boundary yet -- authd",
    "mints a single Full token rather than a linked Limited/Full pair -- so an",
    "administrator's shell runs at High with these privileges for its whole",
    "life. That is a known, deliberate gap; see the linked-token-pair work.",
    "",
    "NOT GRANTED, and each for its own reason:",
    "",
    "  SeCreateTokenPrivilege       Mints any identity without going near authd,",
    "                               which would make every other control here",
    "                               decorative. authd's alone.",
    "  SeTcbPrivilege               The trusted computing base. authd and peinit.",
    "  SeAssignPrimaryTokenPrivilege  peinit's, for launching services.",
    "",
    "WITHHELD BY DEFAULT -- grantable, but you should have to ask:",
    "",
    "  SeDebugPrivilege             Writes to any process regardless of its",
    "                               integrity label, so it is the single",
    "                               privilege that most directly defeats the",
    "                               integrity boundary. Ordinary administration",
    "                               does not need it; add it to this list when a",
    "                               machine genuinely does.",
    "  SeAuditPrivilege             Emits KMES events. Wants an audit policy",
    "                               decision first.",
    "  SeLockMemoryPrivilege        Rarely needed and a denial-of-service lever.",
    "  SeBindPrivilegedPortPrivilege  Belongs on the service that needs it, not",
    "                               on every administrator.",
    "",
    "-- Locking down ----------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "To forbid a privilege machine-wide whatever any record says, add it to a",
    "DeniedPrivileges REG_MULTI_SZ on the Policy key itself (not on a record).",
    "It is applied after the union, so no record you have not read can defeat",
    "it, and it cannot collide with a principal who happens to be called",
    "'Denied'.",
    "",
    "-- Integrity -------------------------------------------------------------",
    "",
    "Integrity may be a tier name (Untrusted, Low, Medium, High, System) or a",
    "raw REG_DWORD for a level between them, since the kernel compares integrity",
    "numerically. A principal no record names gets Medium.",
    "",
    "The user's own record wins outright; otherwise the maximum across their",
    "groups. So a single account can be pinned DOWN by giving it its own record",
    "-- which a flat maximum could never express -- but a group cannot impose a",
    "floor on a member.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the authd package into /usr/share/regim/; it only applies if an",
    "image opts in via [registry] autoapply in its peiso.toml. The package",
    "proposes, the image decides -- so a hardened image ships its own file here",
    "rather than a different authd."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn" },
    { "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy\\Everyone",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "Privileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege",
            "SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy\\Administrators",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "Privileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "SeChangeNotifyPrivilege",
            "SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege",
            "SeBackupPrivilege",
            "SeRestorePrivilege",
            "SeShutdownPrivilege",
            "SeRemoteShutdownPrivilege",
            "SeSystemtimePrivilege",
            "SeSecurityPrivilege",
            "SeLoadDriverPrivilege",
            "SeImpersonatePrivilege",
            "SeIncreaseQuotaPrivilege",
            "SeIncreaseBasePriorityPrivilege",
            "SeProfileSingleProcessPrivilege"
          ]
        },
        { "name": "Integrity", "type": "sz", "data": "High" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
